      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To demonstrate low back and/or leg pain patient reaction to attendance at a low back wellness school conducted to teach them how to control their back pain in daily living so as to reduce the incidence and severity of their problem."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Sixty-one patients attending the clinic filled out a seven-question form that ranked their opinions of the class based on their feelings and reactions about it."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "The private clinic of the author where a three-part back pain prevention clinic utilizing a slide lecture and patient participation was presented."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS",
          "content": "All suffered from low back and/or leg pain and were invited to attend at the time of their initial examination and report of findings."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTION",
          "content": "None. This is a patient questionnaire only."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES",
          "content": "Immediately following the class, the patients were presented with a seven-question form to answer."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULT",
          "content": "A very positive acceptance of low-back wellness training is evidenced by 95% of the patients feeling it was worth their time to attend and feeling they learned something to prevent reinjury in daily living; 100% felt it worth the doctor's time to present the class."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Low back wellness school is a positive program from the patients' and doctor's viewpoints."
        }
      ]},
